# Manual API requests for the VS Code REST Client extension.
# Run the Go server first (see README.md). For /api/users/me, enable
# PostgreSQL-backed resolution as described in docs/application-user-resolution.md.
# Authentication examples use a real Firebase *user ID token*, not the
# Google OAuth token returned by `gcloud auth application-default`.
#
# To run the authenticated example, refresh a Firebase ID token with
#   scripts/firebase-id-token.sh
# (or obtain one by hand as described in docs/firebase-auth-testing.md). Either
# way, it ends up as this line in a local, ignored `.env`:
#   FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN=<your short-lived Firebase ID token>
#
# The REST Client's {{$dotenv FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN}} variable reads it from `.env`.
# Never commit `.env` or paste tokens into this tracked file.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
# @baseUrl = https://mapmory.app

### Health check — public (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### Authentication — missing bearer token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### Authentication — invalid bearer token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token

### Authentication — wrong scheme (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic invalid-token

### Authentication — valid Firebase user ID token (200)
# Requires FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN in the locally ignored .env file.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN}}

### Application user — missing bearer token (401)
# Requires MAPMORY_ENABLE_DB_USER_RESOLUTION=true in .env (or the process
# environment) when starting the Go server.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me

### Application user — invalid bearer token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token

### Application user — verified Firebase token (200)
# Requires PostgreSQL, applied Goose migrations, and the enabled resolver.
# First request creates the users row if absent; later requests return
# the same internal UUID for the same Firebase UID.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN}}

# WARNING: /api/users/me resolves a persistent application user, but trip
# endpoints are still UNPROTECTED and use process-wide, in-memory storage.
# Successful authentication does not imply trip ownership enforcement.

### List trips — currently public (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/trips

### Create trip — currently public (201)
# @name createTrip
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/trips
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Japan",
  "notes": "Summer trip"
}

### Get the trip created above (200)
# Run "Create trip" first; the server must not have restarted.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/trips/{{createTrip.response.body.$.id}}

### Invalid trip — blank title (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/trips
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "   "
}

### Invalid trip — unknown field (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/trips
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Japan",
  "titel": "typo"
}

### Missing trip — JSON 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/trips/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
